WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.560
- I'm starting to feel it now.

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.450
- Oh my God.

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.283
- Fire!

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.560
(coughing)

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.858
You're shaking!

00:00:06.858 --> 00:00:07.691
- I need some milk.

00:00:07.691 --> 00:00:08.564
I need some milk!

00:00:08.564 --> 00:00:09.835
- [Girl] No!

00:00:09.835 --> 00:00:11.620
(playful music)

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.453
- Hi there!

00:00:12.453 --> 00:00:14.043
I'm Aria, and I love to eat.

00:00:14.043 --> 00:00:17.360
Although not quite as much
as the mukbang performers

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.560
who can be regularly seen
eating large quantities of food

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.280
in front of thousands
upon thousands online.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.020
This phenomenon was born in Korea

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.380
and I'm thinking, what
better way to learn about

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:32.380
the art of the Mukbang, than
by performing one myself?

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.600
Goddamn, it's hot.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:40.760
Blowing up since 2008, mukbangs
feature broadcast jockeys,

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.570
or BJs, who stream
themselves as they consume

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:46.160
large portions of food while
interacting with viewers

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.260
that according to one theory,
eat vicariously through them,

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.470
and to get the proper experience,
I'm meeting with Hyunee,

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:56.430
one of Youtube's most
popular mukbang stars.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:58.793
- Let's dig in 'cause I'm so hungry!

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:02.220
- Mukbang literally means eating show,

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.270
but to me, it's being a
friend to my Hyunee-bees

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:06.940
who are my subscribers.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.100
So this is my kitchen where I normally

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.863
cook all my food for my mukbangs.

00:01:12.863 --> 00:01:14.320
- What would you say is the craziest thing

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.260
you've cooked yourself?

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.460
- The craziest thing is
mozzarella corn dogs.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:19.293
- Did you eat all of them?

00:01:19.293 --> 00:01:20.126
- Yeah.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.193
- All right.

00:01:22.193 --> 00:01:24.587
- Some people who come to my channel say,

00:01:24.587 --> 00:01:26.710
"Her intro is so cringy!"

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:29.240
but I love that I can be more silly

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.400
and just be myself when I build mukbangs.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.986
I think about all these ideas

00:01:33.986 --> 00:01:37.350
and then I start writing
it on the whiteboard.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.500
- So you basically eat food
from all around the world.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.210
- My dad always introduced
me to different types of food

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.240
and that's what my
Hyunee-bees love about me

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:48.760
because I try different types of food.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.760
When I was around six or seven years old,

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.790
my dad fainted and when
we went to the hospital

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.870
the doctor said he only
had six months to live,

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:02.670
but he actually fought for 14 years.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.620
Through mukbangs, I tell my life story

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:09.300
and I get to remember my dad,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:13.060
and get to share all the
food that I shared with him

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:14.570
with my Hyunee-bees.

00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:17.723
So right here is, ta-da!

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.200
My mukbang room!

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.070
- [Aria] This is where the magic happens.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:23.430
- [Hyunee] Yeah, exactly.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.600
- I gotta ask.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.180
Is there a sexual element
to this for some viewers?

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.550
- I think so.

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:32.720
A very few percentage, but I think mostly,

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.710
the slurping sound makes
you wanna eat the food

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:39.010
so it's not too much
of the sexual content.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.910
I think people watch mukbangs

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:43.030
because they wanna make new friends.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:46.320
That's one reason why I
started my mukbang channel.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.240
Mukbang isn't all about filming

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.520
and eating in front of the camera.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:54.810
It's more about helping others
with depression, anxiety,

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.633
and being their companion.

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.720
- [Aria] Having heard more
about Hyunee's process,

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:02.380
I'm now ready to tackle
the mukbang challenge

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:04.100
she has arranged for me.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.550
- The challenge is I'm gonna
try to eat five noodles

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:09.620
and you're gonna try to eat five noodles

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.840
and see who eats it faster.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.960
A lot of people have actually tried this.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.680
I'm surprised that you haven't.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:16.513
- Evan, no!

00:03:16.513 --> 00:03:18.870
I'm actually worried about your insides.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.320
- You're really gonna get a major BTS.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:22.320
- BTS?

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.303
- Booty Tingling Sensation?

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:26.723
- You know what?

00:03:26.723 --> 00:03:29.950
I actually have a little
extra surprise for you.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:30.783
- What?

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:33.180
- I say we grate ourselves

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.580
some Trinidad Scorpion Peppers on time.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.180
- You know what, I actually
have a surprise for you.

00:03:40.054 --> 00:03:41.690
(playful music)

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:45.653
I have the world's hottest chocolate.

00:03:45.653 --> 00:03:46.860
(laughing)

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.100
- Oh.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:51.298
We do the challenge, we grate
a little bit of this on top,

00:03:51.298 --> 00:03:52.156
and then--
- And then we could

00:03:52.156 --> 00:03:52.989
try this after.

00:03:52.989 --> 00:03:53.822
Dessert.
- Dessert.

00:03:53.822 --> 00:03:54.655
Okay.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:57.680
- We're gonna boil two eggs.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:03:59.080
One for me, one for you.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:00.760
It helps coat your stomach

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.763
before you eat anything spicy.

00:04:03.626 --> 00:04:06.960
So in Korea, we crack each other's eggs.

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.053
Can I show you?

00:04:11.426 --> 00:04:12.259
Oh my gosh!

00:04:12.259 --> 00:04:13.210
- That egg was definitely

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.970
not cooked all the way.
- [Hyunee] I'm so sorry!

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.553
(upbeat music)

00:04:23.247 --> 00:04:26.040
- And after preparing a
dish that could easily feed,

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.880
and possibly kill, a family of eight,

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.413
the stage is set for us to begin.

00:04:32.595 --> 00:04:35.270
(upbeat music)

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:36.850
- Hello, Hyunee-bees
it's your girl, Hyunee,

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.310
and this is.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.600
- [Aria] Aria!

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:42.223
- So let's dig in 'cause I'm so hungry!

00:04:43.735 --> 00:04:45.350
(clapping)

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:48.013
- Three, two, one.

00:04:49.194 --> 00:04:51.350
(playful music)

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.868
I was starting okay,

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:54.871
but then the heat started
really building up in my mouth.

00:04:54.871 --> 00:04:56.654
How are you feeling?

00:04:56.654 --> 00:04:57.487
(mumbling)

00:04:57.487 --> 00:04:59.520
You okay?

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.650
I definitely bit into some of that pepper

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.602
'cause I felt some of the flakes,

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:04.435
and it just snowballed.

00:05:04.435 --> 00:05:05.268
- You're crying!

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.450
My tongue's burning now.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.223
- My lips are really feeling it.

00:05:10.496 --> 00:05:11.530
I was at the point where I
couldn't even put my mouth

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:13.750
'cause my lips were on fire.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:14.600
- You're shaking!

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:16.750
- I need some milk!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.310
I need some milk!

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.580
- No!

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.680
Already?

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:21.513
- I'm not gonna drink it yet.

00:05:21.513 --> 00:05:23.010
I grab Devy and Christian.

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.080
Christian, get in here.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:24.993
They jumped in.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:26.773
How is it?

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:31.494
So you usually talk about life, right?

00:05:31.494 --> 00:05:32.327
(Hyunee mumbling)

00:05:32.327 --> 00:05:33.160
Cool.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.370
I was like, you know, screw it.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.713
I'm just gonna wolf down as much as I can.

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:38.693
- Whoa.

00:05:38.693 --> 00:05:39.863
- [Christian] There we go.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.194
- And that may have been

00:05:44.194 --> 00:05:45.523
(alarm ringing)
a very foolish choice.

00:05:47.125 --> 00:05:47.958
- Oh my God!

00:05:47.958 --> 00:05:49.890
- Because then right after that,

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.510
out came the chocolate chili.

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:54.110
I'd like to dedicate this to
all the mukbangers out there.

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:56.577
Let's stay mukbanging.

00:05:56.577 --> 00:05:58.377
And it all went downhill from there.

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:02.149
Oh no, I'm feeling it.

00:06:02.149 --> 00:06:02.982
I'm feeling it.
- I feel it now.

00:06:02.982 --> 00:06:04.256
